<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Banu Taghlib</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Banu Taghlib were an Arab tribe of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rabia">Rabi'a</a> group, settled in the Jazira of upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> in late antiquity. Largely Christian before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>, many kept their faith under the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphs</a>, who taxed them on special terms. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamdanid-dynasty">Hamdanid dynasty</a>, which ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mosul">Mosul</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a> in the 10th century, came from the tribe.</p></div>
